      "problem": "Write the equations of the vertical and horizontal lines that pass through the point $B.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the vertical line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The **equation** of the horizontal line is \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "The coordinates of $B$ are $(4,1).$\n\n- Since the vertical line should pass through $(4,1)$, the $x$-value for every point on the line is $4.$ Hence, the equation of that line is \n\n$$\nx=4.\n$$\n\n- Since the horizontal line should pass through $(4,1)$, the $y$-value for every point on the line is $1.$ Hence, the equation of that line is \n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$",
