    "q-167069": {
      "dom_id": "question-167069",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "What is the length of $\\overset{―}{AB}?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $|\\overset{―}{AB}|\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "From the picture, the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-2,3)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(4,1),$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\overset{―}{AB}| & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(4-(-2))^{2}+(1-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(6)^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{40} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
