    "q-167073": {
      "dom_id": "question-167073",
      "name": null,
      "problem": "Calculate the $x$-intercept of the line $\\overset{↔}{AB}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $x\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "Previously, we found that $\\overset{↔}{AB}$ has equation\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\nAt the $x$-intercept, the $y$-coordinate is equal to $0.$ So, we can substitute $y=0$ into the equation and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{1}{3}x+\\frac{7}{3} \\\\ 0 & =-x+7 \\\\ x & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the $x$-intercept is $x=7.$ The coordinates of the $x$-intercept are $(7,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "",
